# pyproject.toml packaging rules

- Store package metadata and runtime dependencies in the PEP 621 `[project]`
  table.
- Store development and deployment dependency sets in PEP 735
  `[dependency-groups]`.
- Use uv for locking, environment synchronization, command execution, builds,
  and requirements exports.
- Use Hatchling only as the PEP 517 build backend. Keep the wheel package and
  forced-module mappings in `[tool.hatch.build.targets.wheel]`.
- Keep console entry points in `[project.scripts]`.
- Commit the single `uv.lock` file and use `--locked` in reproducible workflows.
